# T12-A2 repeated runs (final state).
#
# Finding 1 (blocking): ssr_outbound_wrong_password_never_reaches_the_target could
# hang. Two causes: (a) the peer's address read was unbounded, so a wrong password
# decrypting to a domain/IPv6 type waited for bytes the client never sends while the
# client waited for the echo; (b) an intermittent random_head misalignment (the CRC
# head-boundary check also matches one byte short for some lengths, and the ascending
# scan took that shorter boundary) made the peer misparse the auth frame.
# Fixes: the peer's address read and dial are bounded (2 s, recorded as address-error);
# the client roundtrip is bounded (10 s positive, 5 s negative); the random_head
# boundary search now runs from the longest candidate on both sides.
