#     peer saw the head one byte short: "detected length=98 buffered=103",
#     then "auth_chain wrong client hash");
#   - the head boundary check was proven to admit the short boundary for ~0.3%
#     of random lengths (`random_head_length_picks_the_real_boundary` pins a
#     concrete vector);
#   - after the longest-first scan: 300 pinned-client connections, 0 failures;
#     10 full Rust plugin-matrix runs (6 random_head cases each), 0 failures.
# The only residual ambiguity is a TCP split exactly one byte before the head
# end on a length that admits the short boundary; the pinned format carries no
# explicit head length. It did not reproduce after the fix.
